From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] namespace: do not pass textual hidepid= without fsopen()

mount_procfs() decides whether to pass hidepid= and subset=pid with
mount_option_supported() != 0. That function returns -EAGAIN, meaning "cannot
tell", when the kernel has no fsopen(), and -EAGAIN is not 0, so the options
are passed anyway.

A kernel without fsopen() (added in 5.2) is older than 5.8, where the textual
hidepid= values and subset= appeared, so the proc mount is refused. On the
LuneOS Linux 3.4 Halium machines the kernel logs

  proc: unrecognized mount option "hidepid=invisible" or missing value

and every unit with ProtectProc=invisible or ProcSubset=pid, which includes
systemd-userdbd, systemd-hostnamed and systemd-localed, fails with EINVAL in
its mount namespace setup.

Only add the options when mount_option_supported() reports > 0.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [systemd's minimum kernel is much newer than 3.4]
---
--- a/src/core/namespace.c
+++ b/src/core/namespace.c
@@ -1434,14 +1434,17 @@
                  * fsopen()/fsconfig() was also backported on some distros which allows us to detect
                  * hidepid=/subset= support in even more scenarios. */
 
-                if (mount_option_supported("proc", "hidepid", hpv) != 0) {
+                /* > 0, not != 0: a kernel without fsopen() makes this return -EAGAIN ("cannot tell"),
+                 * and such a kernel is older than 5.8, which is where the textual hidepid= and subset=
+                 * values appeared. Passing them anyway makes the proc mount fail with EINVAL. */
+                if (mount_option_supported("proc", "hidepid", hpv) > 0) {
                         opts = strjoin("hidepid=", hpv);
                         if (!opts)
                                 return -ENOMEM;
                 }
 
                 if (p->proc_subset == PROC_SUBSET_PID &&
-                    mount_option_supported("proc", "subset", "pid") != 0)
+                    mount_option_supported("proc", "subset", "pid") > 0)
                         if (!strextend_with_separator(&opts, ",", "subset=pid"))
                                 return -ENOMEM;
         }
